IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4.
-- SCHEDULE 11: circumstances in which periods of entitlement to statutory sick pay do not arise. The converter dropped the paragraph numbers.
-- The Schedule's opening sentence is paragraph 1 and the Treasury-concurrence sentence is paragraph 1A; "paragraph 2 below" names "The circumstances are that—"
-- as paragraph 2, whose limbs (a), (b), (c) and (ii), (iii) are blank. The definition of "relevant date" and the five paragraphs after it carry no numbers in the text, so
-- they are labelled by what they qualify (for example "the exception to paragraph 2(d)(i)"): the numbers they would bear are not in this rendering.
-- Seam S32: two of the circumstances turn on s 153(12) and s 171(1) (statutory maternity pay), whose answers are taken as inputs.

§ `Schedule 11 -- circumstances in which a period of entitlement to statutory sick pay does not arise`

§§ `The relevant date`

-- Seam found (not in PLAN.md section 5): the answer belongs to s 153 (ssc6), so the input is named with that label.
-- "In this Schedule 'relevant date' means the date on which a period of entitlement would begin in accordance with section 153 above if this Schedule did not prevent it arising."
-- src:5686 | In this Schedule “relevant date” means the date on which a period of entitlement would begin in accordance with section 153 above if this Schedule did not prevent it arising.
@ref sch 11 relevant date (src:5686)
GIVEN `s 153 the date on which a period of entitlement would begin if this Schedule did not prevent it arising` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`sch 11 the relevant date` MEANS `s 153 the date on which a period of entitlement would begin if this Schedule did not prevent it arising`

§§ `Paragraph 2(d) -- incapacity benefit in the previous 57 days`

-- 2(d)(i): in the period of 57 days ending immediately before the relevant date the employee had at least one day on which he was entitled to incapacity benefit (or would have been
-- so entitled had he satisfied the contribution conditions mentioned in section 30A(2)(a)). The 57 days are the relevant date minus 57 days up to the day before it.
-- src:5674 | The circumstances are that—
-- src:5678 | (d) in the period of 57 days ending immediately before the relevant date the employee had at least one day on which—
-- src:5679 | (i) he was entitled to incapacity benefit (or would have been so entitled had he satisfied the contribution conditions mentioned in section 30A(2)(a) above), ...
@ref sch 11 para 2 (d)(i) (src:5674) (src:5678-5679)
GIVEN `the relevant date` IS A DATE
      `the days on which the employee was entitled to incapacity benefit, or would have been so entitled had the contribution conditions mentioned in section 30A(2)(a) been satisfied` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 11 para 2(d)(i) the employee had such a day in the 57 days` MEANS
    any (GIVEN day YIELD (day AT LEAST (`the relevant date` MINUS 57)) AND (day AT MOST (`the relevant date` MINUS 1))) `the days on which the employee was entitled to incapacity benefit, or would have been so entitled had the contribution conditions mentioned in section 30A(2)(a) been satisfied`

-- The two exceptions to 2(d)(i): (1) it does not apply if, at the relevant date, the employee is over pensionable age and is not entitled to incapacity benefit; (2) it ceases to apply if, at any
-- time after the relevant date, the employee is over pensionable age and is not entitled to incapacity benefit. (3) "pensionable age" is borrowed from the Pensions Act 1995 (the core's
-- `date of attaining pensionable age`), and "over" is s 173(a): the employee is over the age on and after the day of attaining it.
-- src:5689 | (1) Paragraph 2(d)(i) above does not apply if, at the relevant date, the employee is over pensionable age and is not entitled to incapacity benefit.
-- src:5690 | (2) Paragraph 2(d)(i) above ceases to apply if, at any time after the relevant date, the employee is over pensionable age and is not entitled to incapacity benefit.
-- src:5691 | (3) In this paragraph “pensionable age” has the meaning given by the rules in paragraph 1 of Schedule 4 to the Pensions Act 1995.
@ref sch 11 exception to para 2(d)(i) (src:5689-5691)
GIVEN `paragraph 2(d)(i) is otherwise met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant date` IS A DATE
      `the date the employee attains pensionable age` IS A DATE
      `the employee is entitled to incapacity benefit at the relevant date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days after the relevant date on which the employee is not entitled to incapacity benefit` IS A LIST OF DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 11 para 2(d)(i) applies on the day` MEANS
    `paragraph 2(d)(i) is otherwise met` AND NOT (disappliedAtRelevantDate OR ceased)
    WHERE
        disappliedAtRelevantDate MEANS (`the relevant date` AT LEAST `the date the employee attains pensionable age`) AND NOT `the employee is entitled to incapacity benefit at the relevant date`
        ceased MEANS any (GIVEN t YIELD (t GREATER THAN `the relevant date`) AND (t AT LEAST `the date the employee attains pensionable age`) AND (t AT MOST day)) `the days after the relevant date on which the employee is not entitled to incapacity benefit`

§§ `Paragraph 2(dd) -- employment and support allowance in the previous 85 days`

-- 2(dd): in the period of 85 days ending immediately before the relevant date the employee had at least one day on which he was entitled to an employment and support allowance (or would have been so
-- entitled had he satisfied the requirements in section 1(2) of the Welfare Reform Act 2007).
-- src:5682 | (dd) in the period of 85 days ending immediately before the relevant date the employee had at least one day on which he was entitled to an employment and support allowance (or would have been so entitled had he satisfied the requirements in section 1(2) of the Welfare Reform Act 2007.
@ref sch 11 para 2(dd) (src:5682)
GIVEN `the relevant date` IS A DATE
      `the days on which the employee was entitled to an employment and support allowance, or would have been so entitled had the requirements in section 1(2) of the Welfare Reform Act 2007 been satisfied` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 11 para 2(dd) the circumstance applies` MEANS
    any (GIVEN day YIELD (day AT LEAST (`the relevant date` MINUS 85)) AND (day AT MOST (`the relevant date` MINUS 1))) `the days on which the employee was entitled to an employment and support allowance, or would have been so entitled had the requirements in section 1(2) of the Welfare Reform Act 2007 been satisfied`

§§ `Paragraph 2(f) -- no work done under the contract of service`

-- The joining rule for 2(f): "if an employee enters into a contract of service which is to take effect not more than 8 weeks after the date on which a previous contract of service entered
-- into by him with the same employer ceased to have effect, the two contracts shall be treated as one." Work under the previous contract then counts as work under the contract.
-- src:5692 | For the purposes of paragraph 2(f) above, if an employee enters into a contract of service which is to take effect not more than 8 weeks after the date on which a previous contract of service entered into by him with the same employer ceased to have effect, the two contracts shall be treated as one.
@ref sch 11 joining rule for para 2(f) (src:5692)
GIVEN `the employee has done no work for the employer under the new contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee has done no work for the employer under the previous contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the previous contract of service with the same employer ceased to have effect` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the new contract of service is to take effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 11 para 2(f) the employee has done no work for the employer under the contract of service` MEANS
    `the employee has done no work for the employer under the new contract of service` AND ((NOT joined) OR `the employee has done no work for the employer under the previous contract of service`)
    WHERE
        joined MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day the previous contract of service with the same employer ceased to have effect`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST ceased THEN (Day `the day the new contract of service is to take effect`) MINUS (Day ceased) AT MOST 56

-- 2(f): "the employee has done no work for his employer under his contract of service" (with the two contracts treated as one under the rule above).
-- src:5683 | (f) the employee has done no work for his employer under his contract of service;
@ref sch 11 para 2(f) (src:5683)
GIVEN `the employee has done no work for the employer under the contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 11 para 2(f) the circumstance applies` MEANS `the employee has done no work for the employer under the contract of service`

§§ `Paragraph 2(g) -- stoppage of work due to a trade dispute`

-- 2(g): "on the relevant date there is ... a stoppage of work due to a trade dispute at the employee's place of employment". It does not apply to an employee who proves that at no time
-- on or before the relevant date did he have a direct interest in the trade dispute in question.
-- src:5684 | (g) on the relevant date there is ... a stoppage of work due to a trade dispute at the employee’s place of employment;
-- src:5693 | Paragraph 2(g) above does not apply in the case of an employee who proves that at no time on or before the relevant date did he have a direct interest in the trade dispute in question.
@ref sch 11 para 2(g) and its exception (src:5684) (src:5693)
GIVEN `on the relevant date there is a stoppage of work due to a trade dispute at the employee’s place of employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee proves that at no time on or before the relevant date did he have a direct interest in the trade dispute in question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 11 para 2(g) the circumstance applies` MEANS
    `on the relevant date there is a stoppage of work due to a trade dispute at the employee’s place of employment` AND NOT `the employee proves that at no time on or before the relevant date did he have a direct interest in the trade dispute in question`

§§ `Paragraph 2(h) -- pregnancy and the disqualifying period`

-- 2(h): "the employee is, or has been, pregnant and the relevant date falls within the disqualifying period (within the meaning of section 153(12) above)" (S32). It does not apply to an
-- employee who has been pregnant if her pregnancy terminated, before the beginning of the disqualifying period, otherwise than by confinement (section 171(1), S32).
-- src:5685 | (h) the employee is, or has been, pregnant and the relevant date falls within the disqualifying period (within the meaning of section 153(12) above).
-- src:5694 | Paragraph 2(h) above does not apply in relation to an employee who has been pregnant if her pregnancy terminated, before the beginning of the disqualifying period, otherwise than by confinement (as defined for the purposes of statutory maternity pay in section 171(1) above).
@ref sch 11 para 2(h) and its exception (src:5685) (src:5694)
GIVEN `the employee is, or has been, pregnant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 153(12) the relevant date falls within the disqualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `her pregnancy terminated, before the beginning of the disqualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 171(1) the pregnancy terminated otherwise than by confinement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 11 para 2(h) the circumstance applies` MEANS
    `the employee is, or has been, pregnant` AND `s 153(12) the relevant date falls within the disqualifying period` AND NOT (`her pregnancy terminated, before the beginning of the disqualifying period` AND `s 171(1) the pregnancy terminated otherwise than by confinement`)

§§ `Paragraph 1 -- the rule`

-- 1: "A period of entitlement does not arise in relation to a particular period of incapacity for work in any of the circumstances set out in paragraph 2 below or in such other circumstances as
-- may be prescribed." 1A: regulations under paragraph 1 must be made with the Treasury's concurrence (inert, machinery). If a circumstance applies, none arises (FALSE); if none does,
-- the Schedule does not itself say that one arises (NOTHING): section 153 decides.
-- src:5672 | A period of entitlement does not arise in relation to a particular period of incapacity for work in any of the circumstances set out in paragraph 2 below or in such other circumstances as may be prescribed.
@ref sch 11 para 1 (src:5672)
GIVEN `paragraph 2(d)(i) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph 2(dd) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph 2(f) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph 2(g) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph 2(h) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of such other circumstances as may be prescribed applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 11 para 1 a period of entitlement may arise` MEANS
    IF `paragraph 2(d)(i) applies` OR `paragraph 2(dd) applies` OR `paragraph 2(f) applies` OR `paragraph 2(g) applies` OR `paragraph 2(h) applies` OR `one of such other circumstances as may be prescribed applies`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A period of entitlement does not arise ... in any of the circumstances set out in paragraph 2 below or in such other circumstances as may be prescribed"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Schedule only removes periods of entitlement; section 153 says when one begins
